# Sphinx Documentation Rules

## When This Applies
- Creating or editing Sphinx docs under `docs/`
- Adding/updating `docs/conf.py`, `.rst`, or MyST Markdown pages
- Wiring autodoc to project scripts (`train.py`, `detect_simple.py`, `predict_*_test.py`, `evaluate_test_predictions.py`)

## Layout
Prefer a flat, script-oriented tree (no web API docs):

```text
docs/
├── conf.py
├── index.rst                 # or index.md with MyST
├── usage/
│   ├── training.rst
│   ├── detection.rst
│   ├── prediction.rst
│   └── evaluation.rst
├── api/
│   └── modules.rst           # autodoc stubs
└── _static/                  # optional: confusion_matrix.png, training_history.png
```

- Keep English as the Sphinx primary language; Persian narrative stays in `README_FA.md` unless the user asks for bilingual Sphinx
- Link out to root `README.md` / `README_FA.md` instead of duplicating long setup text

## Extensions
Enable only what you need:

```python
extensions = [
    "sphinx.ext.autodoc",
    "sphinx.ext.napoleon",      # Google-style docstrings (match python-base)
    "sphinx.ext.viewcode",
    "sphinx.ext.intersphinx",   # optional: Python / PyTorch refs
]
```

- Prefer **Napoleon + Google** docstrings over NumPy style
- MyST (`myst_parser`) is OK if the user wants Markdown pages; otherwise stick to `.rst`
- Do **not** add FastAPI / HTTP / OpenAPI Sphinx extensions

## `conf.py` Conventions
- `project = "densNet"`
- `author` / `copyright` as already used in the repo (or leave placeholders if unset)
- Set `sys.path` so autodoc can import top-level scripts:

```python
import sys
from pathlib import Path

ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))
```

- Autodoc defaults:
  - `autodoc_typehints = "description"`
  - `napoleon_google_docstring = True`
  - `napoleon_numpy_docstring = False`
- Theme: `sphinx_rtd_theme` or Alabaster; do not add a heavy custom theme unless asked
- Exclude build artifacts: `_build`, `.venv`, `slm`, datasets

## What To Document
| Topic | Source of truth |
|-------|-----------------|
| Classes / order | `CLASS_NAMES = ["dentin", "enamel", "pulp"]` |
| Checkpoint | `slm/resolution_best_densenet_model.pth` |
| Train data | `segmented_dental_adiography/{train,valid,test}/` |
| External tests | `image-testing/{dentin,enamel,pulp}_test/` |
| Metrics | Precision, Recall, Accuracy, F1 (same formulas as evaluate script) |
| Plots | Reuse `training_history.png`, `confusion_matrix.png` via `_static/` or repo-root links |

Document **CLI usage and public functions**, not private training loops line-by-line.

## Autodoc Hygiene
- Module docstrings at the top of every documented script
- Public functions: Args / Returns / Raises (Google style)
- Skip undocumented private helpers (`_foo`) unless they are part of the public contract
- If a script is not import-safe (runs on import), fix with `if __name__ == "__main__":` before enabling autodoc on it — do not wrap autodoc hacks around side-effectful imports

## Build
```bash
cd docs && sphinx-build -b html . _build/html
# or: make html
```

- Output belongs in `docs/_build/` (gitignored)
- Do not commit `_build/`, large datasets, or `*.pth` into docs
- Optional: add a short “Building the docs” subsection to `README.md` when Sphinx is introduced

## Writing Style
- Imperative, short sections; one purpose per page
- Prefer code blocks for commands the user can copy
- Keep class index order and metric formulas consistent with `global` / DenseNet rules
- When adding figures, use existing project plots; do not invent metrics screenshots

## Do Not
- Scaffold FastAPI / REST API reference pages
- Change class labels or DenseNet121 defaults “for documentation clarity”
- Vendor Sphinx themes or large binary assets into git
- Duplicate full evaluation tables in both README and Sphinx unless one clearly links to the other
